WEBVTT

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.710
Is there an event going on?

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.240
What is that?

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.050
Mr. Kururu!

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.420
The Kalta Festival?

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.690
Yes. It's been held for a long time.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.320
I attended the festival a century ago.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.480
Wow.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.850
And the greatest highlight 
of all is the Hunting Festival.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:38.990
Hunting Festival?

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:42.130
Skilled archers enter the 
woods to shoot beasts.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:46.160
Wapow! It's incredibly intense.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.060
Wapow!

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.350
I'm sure it's quite the spectacle.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.560
For the past several years, an elf 
named Mr. Kururu has won every year.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.510
Kururu? That guy?

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.570
Wel...come?

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.730
<i>It's an elf.</i>

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.790
I...

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.750
I want to put my brother to shame!

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.960
Huh? What?

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.270
<b>Drugstore</b>

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.270
<b>In Another World</b>

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.990
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 1
Come Here Beast Lure</b>

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.640
You want to put your brother to shame?

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.350
I am Ririka, Kururu's younger sister.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.350
<b>Ririka</b>

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:57.580
Kururu? Oh, you mean the popular Mr. Kururu 
who wins the Hunting Festival every year?

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:01.360
Yes. But starting this year, 
my brother will be running the event

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.730
rather than participating in the hunt.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.080
Oh... I see.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:09.460
So I will be participating in his place.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:10.970
Uh-huh.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:14.960
I heard there's an incredible 
alchemist in this town named Reiji.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.970
I'm not alchemist, I'm a pharmacist.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.510
And you should know that I can't make a 
medicine that will make you a better archer.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.550
What?!

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:26.730
<i>She really was planning to ask for one.</i>

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.720
I was actually hoping you could 
make a medicine that would make

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.140
a terrible archer like myself win!

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.690
I can't do that.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.780
And it sounds even harder 
than just making a medicine

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.290
that improves your archery skill—

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.550
But I heard you can make any medicine!

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.400
Medicines can't fix everything!

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:46.910
If you want to become better with a bow, 
why don't you have your brother teach you?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.910
My brother always treats me like a child.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.670
He says archery is a bit 
too difficult for me.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:58.050
So you came here for a medicine 
that would do something about that?

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.190
I want to put my brother to shame.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:07.050
If I win the Hunting Festival, 
he'll have to recognize my skills.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.390
Huh? Hold on.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:10.720
Ow.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.690
Oh, sorry.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.900
<i>She already worked hard doing what she could.</i>

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.460
<i>She came to me because that wasn't enough.</i>

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.110
Fine. I'll help you.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.200
What? Really?!

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:28.590
But I can't make a medicine unless 
I know how skilled you are.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.690
Good point.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:36.040
Also, I can't make you a medicine that will 
make you win or make you a better archer.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:39.250
All my medicine can do 
is support your skills.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:40.850
I understand.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:54.590
Woof, woof.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.500
Wh-What? If you're got something 
to say, spit it out.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.900
I-I know I suck.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.420
Let me see your hands.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:07.780
Wait, wha—

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.460
If you're in pain, you should say so.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:14.830
If saying so would make me a 
better archer, then I would.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:15.710
Noela.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:16.410
Woof?

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:17.570
Bring me a potion.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.150
Woof.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.150
Here, take a sip of this.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.460
This medicine recovers stamina.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.250
It should have some effect 
on cuts and blisters, too.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.770
I never said it hurt.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.460
You should accept the kindness of others.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:40.670
It's tasty.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.340
You're starting to hit the target.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:50.780
It's not like I couldn't hit it 
at all to begin with.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.940
Even so, if this is how you 
perform with a stationary target,

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.470
with the unstable footing of the 
forest and a moving target...

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:01.000
Noela, you can shoot a bow?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.390
Woof?

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.630
Archery isn't so simple 
that an amateur can just—

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:10.470
Woof! Master, I hit it!

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.780
That's amazing, Noela.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.220
H-How did she do that so easily?

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.580
Woof.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.140
Woof!

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.100
Woof!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.100
Woof!

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.930
Master, archery is fun.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:28.200
Ms. Noela, you're going to crush 
the spirit of that elf over there.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.200
Actually, it's already been 
crushed. Give it a rest.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:31.660
Woof?

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:36.390
I know I'm a trash elf who sucks at archery.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.370
She's clearly getting depressed!

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:42.840
Uh... Okay, why don't we measure the 
distance at which you can hit the target?

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.190
What?

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:51.470
Here? This distance?

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.360
No, calm down. I decided to help this girl.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.430
Is there a problem?

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:03.090
There's no way beasts would come within 
shooting distance or stand still for you.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:04.980
Actually, that might work.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.220
What? Did you come up with an idea?

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:09.600
I'm going to have you 
practice with a short bow.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:10.950
A short bow?

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:18.070
It certainly may improve my accuracy at 
short range, but only children use short bows.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.890
Can a terrible archer afford 
to worry about appearances?

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:25.130
That's our plan. In other words,

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.950
if you can improve your 
accuracy with a short bow

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:30.220
and hit targets within a few meters...

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.510
Then I'm guaranteed to win!

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.480
It's done!

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:08.480
Woof!

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.840
Master, this smell will definitely work.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:19.680
I hereby announce the opening 
of this year's Hunting Festival!

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:23.160
We've been waiting!

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.970
Look. Ririka's using a short bow, 
when she's not even a child.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.530
And she's Kururu's sister.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:32.970
Pathetic.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.410
Let the hunt begin!

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.800
<i>I'll definitely put him to shame!</i>

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.870
<i>The hunt ends at sundown.</i>

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:58.760
<i>My brother won last year 
with a record of 16 beasts.</i>

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.740
<i>That's my target.</i>

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:05.940
Open that bag at the location we 
picked out beforehand, and then...

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:18.570
They really came!

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.620
This lure will draw beasts to you.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.980
Fire your arrows once they come within range.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.000
That's all you have to do.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:35.970
<b>Come Here Beast Lure</b>

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.760
<i>Come Here Beast Lure.</i>

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:36.050
<i>A very powerful medicine that produces a 
smell attractive to monsters and beasts.</i>

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:39.750
Calm down.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.070
Draw them to you.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:43.120
Fire your bow at the 
distance we practiced at.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.530
<i>Now!</i>

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.630
I did it! That's one!

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.220
Huh?

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.040
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:59.360
<i>Here, the beasts will approach in 
single file while avoiding obstacles.</i>

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:07.460
You're not going to go hunt them. 
They're going to come to you.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.380
It's just like Reiji said!

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:17.840
Don't be scared.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:19.420
I'm not scared!

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:21.790
Huh? What's that sound?

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:26.430
What?! A whole bunch of them came?!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:31.660
This medicine is too effective!

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:38.920
There's no end to them!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.580
This year's winner is Ririka!

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:49.900
She set a new Hunting Festival 
record with 89 beasts hunted.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:54.560
We honor the champion Ririka 
with a commemorative—

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:56.090
Huh? Ririka?

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:04.510
<i>During the hunt, I always heard 
Reiji's voice in my head.</i>

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.750
<i>It encouraged me.</i>

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:28.200
<i>I want to tell him that 
it's all thanks to him.</i>

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:30.700
<i>And then, I'm sure that...</i>

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:34.000
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:47.110
Reiji.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.910
Mr. Reiji, which shelf 
does this medicine go on?

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:54.210
Oh, that goes...

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:57.240
Wait until you hear what Ms. Noela was doing.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:11:59.690
What in the world?

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.490
Woof? What's wrong, Ririka?

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:10.990
Oh, um... I wanted to thank Reiji.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.540
Master, Ririka is here.

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:15.630
Huh?

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:17.630
There's nobody here.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:18.570
Woof?

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:26.310
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:33.020
<i>I think... I think... I'm in love with him.</i>

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:42.670
Excuse me.

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:43.920
Where is the owner?

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:44.960
Right here.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.030
<b>Kururu</b>

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:47.480
Mr. Kururu.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:50.580
You're the owner of the shop?

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.830
What an adorable little boy you are.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.910
Give me a break.

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:57.000
So can I help you with something?

00:12:57.390 --> 00:13:03.420
Yes. I'm here to thank the alchemist 
who helped my sister win today.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.040
I'm telling you, I'm a pharmacist.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.390
Anyway, Ms. Ririka won, then? That's great.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.940
My sister said it was all thanks to you.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:17.600
Oh...

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.840
I'm sure we'll meet again, Reiji.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:21.440
Personal space!

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:23.630
See you then.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.340
What was that about?

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:31.040
Mr. Reiji, are you busy right now?

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.940
No. Is something up?

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:37.390
I wanted to go out with you and Ms. Noela.

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:41.100
Oh, right. I always ask you 
to watch the store alone. And?

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:45.920
When I set foot outside the store,
I immediately return to the living room.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.590
Huh? What does that mean?

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.810
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 2
Mother's Brooch</b>

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:53.530
I'm ready over here.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:54.810
Okay.

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:04.490
I'm over here.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:09.740
No matter how many times I try, 
I always end up back on this sofa.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:15.550
This was originally your house.
Is there some reason this is happening?

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:20.460
I'll probably never leave this house again.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:28.340
Cheer up. Maybe someday you'll suddenly 
gain the ability to go outside.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.580
Mina, what's wrong?

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:32.010
Ms. Noela!

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.220
Fluffy...

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.430
Fluffy...

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:39.140
Fluffy...

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:43.150
If you always return to this 
spot, then this sofa...

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.310
No, is it something beneath it?

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:52.190
Which means it's beneath the floor?

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:56.390
Hey, Mina. Was this room ever remodeled?

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:57.830
Yes, it was.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.130
The family that lived here right after

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:02.420
I became its guardian 
spirit remodeled it once.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.030
Hmm...

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:06.210
Did you call?

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:07.950
Woof.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:21.310
All done! Let me know if you need me again!

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:27.030
Is there something beneath here?

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:31.480
I think we'll find something related to Mina.

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:34.010
A ladder?

00:15:43.530 --> 00:15:45.200
What room is this?

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.500
Was this Mina's mother's room?

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:06.110
<b>Fleuret Family Brooch</b>

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.860
<i>Fleuret Family Brooch.</i>

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:05.420
<i>An expensive piece of jewelry 
set with a green garnet.</i>

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.360
The Fleuret Family...

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:12.990
Do you recognize this?

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.080
My mother gave this to me.

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:21.040
Since it was precious, I asked my 
mother to hold on to it for me.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:25.000
Maybe that's the thing pulling 
you back to this spot.

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:31.900
Mina, I'm ready.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:33.380
Okay.

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:43.410
I'm sorry for crushing you, Mr. Reiji!

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:46.440
Just like I thought, once you move a 
certain distance away from this brooch,

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.550
you teleport back to it.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:49.690
Which means...

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:55.630
Come on, Mina.

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.410
But what if—

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.010
Woof!

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:11.800
Hooray! I'm outside!

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:17.680
I can go shopping or do whatever 
else on my own! Mr. Reiji!

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:21.130
If you keep the brooch in your 
pocket while you walk around,

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:22.850
you won't be bound to the house.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:26.520
Now the three of us can visit 
all kinds of places together.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:31.350
Get off of me! We're outdoors!

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:34.430
I can go anywhere!

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:36.400
Why are you crying?

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:39.620
Because I'm happy!

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:42.570
Me, too!

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:46.340
Mr. Reiji, I'm so happy.

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:48.140
Me, too!

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:50.070
Yeah. Me, too.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:57.470
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 3
Stomach Acheless</b>

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.190
What's the matter, Rolling Noela?

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:03.730
Master, my stomach hurts.

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:05.050
A stomachache?

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:06.940
Did you eat something weird?

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:08.600
I didn't eat anything weird.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:12.070
There were nuts in the road. I ate those.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.400
That's what you call "something weird."

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:19.360
Mr. Reiji and Ms. Noela, lunch is ready.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.720
I don't want any.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:24.780
Oh, what's wrong? How unusual.

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.450
Her stomach hurts, apparently.

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:29.420
You ate something you found 
in the road, didn't you?

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:31.050
I'm impressed you knew.

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:36.590
I see some unusual shell 
fragments in Ms. Noela's hair.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.400
You did this to yourself, Noela.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:41.290
Master, don't forsake me!

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:43.240
Master...

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:48.560
Okay, okay. I'll make you something 
for your stomachache later.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:53.730
Master... Thank you...

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:58.890
I wonder if there's a good way to stop 
Noela from eating stuff off the ground.

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:01.130
You should scold her.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:03.090
You think that would stop her?

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:08.020
I have a feeling she eats things 
not because she's hungry,

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:11.330
but because she's curious how things taste.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:14.820
They say curiosity killed the cat.

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:17.800
Although in this case, she's a werewolf.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:23.970
These days, she seems to enjoy 
chewing expensive rokushou nuts.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.690
Perhaps that's become a habit of hers.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:31.430
Curiosity and rokushou nuts, huh?

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.900
I'll try making a medicine 
to curb her behavior.

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:37.510
What? You can do that?

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:39.360
It's worth a shot.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:42.320
Master, Master...

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:45.550
Can you promise not to eat 
things off the ground anymore?

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:48.870
Yes! I won't do it again!

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:54.580
<i>Noela, you'll pay dearly 
if you break our promise.</i>

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:06.750
It's done.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:15.650
<b>Stomach Acheless</b>

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.940
<i>Stomach Acheless.</i>

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:15.650
<i>Primarily uses o-Cresol to restore and 
settle the functionality of the intestines.</i>

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:18.550
Noela, this'll fix your 
stomachache. Take this.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.670
Thank you, Master.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:24.030
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.030
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:29.160
Noela, what's the matter? 
You're back already?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:32.290
Master, I broke our promise.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:35.120
I won't eat anything off the ground again.

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:38.040
So bitter. The stuff on 
the ground was so bitter.

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:41.600
Well, what's done is done. Drink this.

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:46.010
Woof! All better!

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:53.730
Mr. Reiji, those were rokushou 
shells stuck to Ms. Noela's body.

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:58.100
Why did eating non-toxic rokushou 
nuts have that effect on her?

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:00.440
It's all part of my strategy.

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:08.780
<b>Bitter α</b>

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:02.350
<i>Bitter α.</i>

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:06.750
<i>A medicine that causes everything 
one eats to taste extremely bitter.</i>

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.780
<i>Not harmful to the body.</i>

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:11.850
You expected Ms. Noela to 
eat things off the ground?

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:14.410
I mixed it into the Stomach Acheless.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:17.040
If she keeps her promise, she'll be fine.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:19.130
But if she doesn't...

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:24.780
I don't like bitter.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:27.550
<b>You ate more?</b>

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:28.680
I hate bitter food.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.720
<i>Later, my Bitter α was used to</i>

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:39.050
<i>deter animals from digging through 
the trash and help beautify the town.</i>

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:43.280
<b>Closing Time</b>

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:48.090
Thank you for visiting Kirio 
Drugstore again today.

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:50.970
Okay, good. Nice work.

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:52.410
Woof, woof.

00:21:58.510 --> 00:21:59.540
It's no use.

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:03.100
I'll never finish.

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:05.010
<b>Next Customer</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Illustration by: Honda Obon</b>
